coroutine, continuation, call/cc and yield

full/undelimited continuation, call/cc capture the whole of rest program,
delimited continuation, callCC capture what is inside callCC, shift/reset, prompt/cotroll

Assembly longjump -> C's goto -> scheme's call/cc (goto with context) -> delimited continuation (only capture a part, callCC in haskell, shift/reset in scheme, yield/send in python)

async/await in python is about parallel function without exchange context, just await asyncio.sleep for yield control
do not exchange variable something, but yield can do exchange context

there're two functions f and g, capture f's rest program as k1, call g with k1, capture g's rest program as k2,
jump back k1 with k2, 

python use yield and send can do the same, after 3.6 python has yield in async, the old way is yield with select/epoll for coroutine

